.TH TECHNOBABBLE 1 "2026-11-05" "Technobabble" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
technobabble, technobabble-terminal \- display animated terminal dashboards
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B technobabble
.RB [ \-s " panes" ]
.RB [ \-d " seconds" ]
.RB [ \-\-classic " | " \-\-studio ]
.RB [ \-\-layout " name" ]
.RB [ \-\-refresh " seconds" ]
.br
.B technobabble
.RB [ \-\-help " | " \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run
.B technobabble
in an interactive terminal to start Classic Mode.
Classic builds a random arrangement of animated panes and periodically reshuffles it.
Studio Mode lets you select, resize, pin, and save panes.
Some panes show live system activity.
Others, such as the three instruments in Relay Watch, simulate a fictional incident.
.B technobabble-terminal
starts the same application.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " panes" "\fR, \fB\-\-splits " panes
Set the target pane count from 1 to 20.
The default is twice the processor count, up to 20.
A small terminal may fit fewer panes.
.TP
.BI \-d " seconds" "\fR, \fB\-\-delay " seconds
Wait this long after the last split before reshuffling.
The range is 1 to 86400 seconds; the default is 10.
.TP
.B \-\-classic
Start in Classic Mode (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-studio
Start in Studio Mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " name"
Start Studio with a built-in or saved layout.
Quote names containing spaces.
Built-in layouts include Relay Watch, System Watch, Process Watch,
Disk Watch, GPU Watch, Network Watch, and Blank Canvas.
.TP
.BI \-\-refresh " seconds"
Set the Studio monitor sampling interval to 1, 2, or 5 seconds.
This option and
.B \-\-layout
each select Studio Mode and cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-classic .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short command reference and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and platform and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
.TP
.BR Q ", " Ctrl-C
Quit. Use Q from the dashboard or Ctrl-C at any time.
.TP
.BR ? ", " F1
Show or hide the on-screen controls.
.TP
.BR S ", " F2
Switch between Classic and Studio.
.TP
.BR Space ", " R
Space pauses or resumes the animation. R reshuffles the panes.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Shift-Tab
In Studio, select the next or previous pane.
.TP
.BR E ", " P ", " B
In Studio, E opens the pane editor, P toggles pinning, and B adjusts dividers.
.TP
.BR W ", " L
In Studio, W saves a layout and L opens one.
.TP
.B Y
In Studio, cycle the selected code pane through scrolling and typing speeds.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start Classic with a target of eight panes and a 15-second reshuffle delay:
.PP
.nf
    technobabble \-s 8 \-d 15
.fi
.PP
Follow a simulated incident or watch real system activity:
.PP
.nf
    technobabble \-\-layout "Relay Watch"
    technobabble \-\-layout "System Watch" \-\-refresh 1
.fi
.PP
Build a dashboard from one pane:
.PP
.nf
    technobabble \-\-layout "Blank Canvas"
.fi
.PP
Press E to edit or split the pane, then W to save the layout.
.SH FILES
On Linux, saved layouts are
.I *.layout
files under
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/technobabble/layouts .
The default is
.IR ~/.local/share/technobabble/layouts .
The macOS preview uses
.IR "~/Library/Application Support/Technobabble/layouts" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TECHNOBABBLE_LAYOUT_DIR
Use this directory for saved layouts in place of the platform default.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
On Linux, use this absolute directory as the base for application data.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
Input or output error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments, a layout that could not be opened, or an unsuitable terminal or platform.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project, downloads, and platform guides:
.UR https://github.com/lordtempis/technobabble
.UE .
